---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/about.css";
---

<BaseLayout title="About | Economic Machine Learning Lab">

<section class="about-hero">
        <div class="about-hero-content">
            <div class="about-kicker">Economic Machine Learning Lab</div>
            <h1>Where Machine Learning Meets Economic Inquiry.</h1>
            <p>The EML Lab develops theory-guided machine learning methods for modern economic data while creating space for research, training, and collaboration.</p>
            <div class="hero-pill-row" aria-label="Core areas">
                <span class="hero-pill">Research</span>
                <span class="hero-pill">Education</span>
                <span class="hero-pill">Collaboration</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <main class="about-container">
        <section class="intro-panel">
            <div>
                <div class="section-label">Our Vision</div>
                <h2>Building methods for the next generation of economic data.</h2>
                <p>The Economic Machine Learning (EML) Lab envisions a future in which empirical economic research is enhanced through innovative methodological approaches, supported by rigorous theories and implemented by efficient procedures.</p>
                <p>For such a future, the Lab aims to develop and disseminate novel frameworks, with relevant theories and methodologies, for machine learning designed specifically to analyze large-dimensional economic data effectively.</p>
            </div>
            <aside class="intro-feature">
                <div>
                    <h3>Core Mission</h3>
                    <p>The EML Lab serves as a hub for research, education, and knowledge exchange across economics, machine learning, and data-driven decision making.</p>
                </div>
                <ul class="feature-list">
                    <li><span></span><div>Develop machine learning methods for large-dimensional economic data.</div></li>
                    <li><span></span><div>Educate students on applicable methodologies and background theories.</div></li>
                    <li><span></span><div>Connect academia and industry around practical prediction and decision problems.</div></li>
                </ul>
            </aside>
        </section>

        <section>
            <div class="section-heading">
                <div>
                    <div class="section-label">EML at a glance</div>
                    <h2>Where economics, data, and computation meet.</h2>
                </div>
                <p>The Lab focuses on methodological development, training, and collaboration in areas where modern economic data require new analytical tools.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="glance-strip">
                <div class="glance-card">
                    <strong>Machine Learning</strong>
                    <p>Methods adapted to economic questions and data structures.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="glance-card">
                    <strong>Econometrics</strong>
                    <p>Theory-grounded approaches for empirical research.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="glance-card">
                    <strong>Large Data</strong>
                    <p>Tools for high-dimensional economic environments.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="glance-card">
                    <strong>Education</strong>
                    <p>Training for students at multiple levels.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="glance-card">
                    <strong>Practice</strong>
                    <p>Knowledge exchange with researchers and practitioners.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section>
            <div class="section-heading">
                <div>
                    <div class="section-label">What We Do</div>
                    <h2>Three connected pillars.</h2>
                </div>
                <p>Each pillar reflects a practical part of the Lab’s identity: developing new methods, training students, and connecting research with real-world decision problems.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="mission-grid">
                <article class="mission-card">
                    <div class="mission-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 19.5V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h12v16H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2.5Z"></path><path d="M8 7h6"></path><path d="M8 11h8"></path></svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Research</h3>
                    <p>Research in the use of machine learning for the effective analysis of large-dimensional economic data, including relevant theories and implementation procedures.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="mission-card">
                    <div class="mission-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 3 2 8l10 5 10-5-10-5Z"></path><path d="M6 10.5V16c0 1.7 2.7 3 6 3s6-1.3 6-3v-5.5"></path></svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Education</h3>
                    <p>Education of students at all levels on machine learning methodologies and background theories applicable to the analysis of large-dimensional economic data.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="mission-card">
                    <div class="mission-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M16 11c1.7 0 3-1.3 3-3s-1.3-3-3-3-3 1.3-3 3 1.3 3 3 3Z"></path><path d="M8 13c1.7 0 3-1.3 3-3S9.7 7 8 7s-3 1.3-3 3 1.3 3 3 3Z"></path><path d="M2 21c.4-3.2 2.7-5 6-5s5.6 1.8 6 5"></path><path d="M14 15c.6-.2 1.3-.3 2-.3 3.3 0 5.6 1.8 6 5"></path></svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Collaboration</h3>
                    <p>Knowledge exchange and collaboration between academia and industry to solve practical problems in decision making and prediction.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="supporters-band">
            <div class="section-label">Our Supporters</div>
            <h2>Supported by institutional and individual partners.</h2>
            <div class="supporters-grid">
                <div class="supporter-card">
                    <h3>Institutional Supporters</h3>
                    <p>College of Arts + Sciences: Indiana University</p>
                    <p>Department of Economics: Indiana University Bloomington</p>
                </div>
                <div class="supporter-card">
                    <h3>Individual Supporters</h3>
                    <p>Ken &amp; Dawn Weakley Foundation</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>

</BaseLayout>